  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a continuous printing process, paper roll is wrapped on a cylindrical core which is free to rotate about a fixed horizontal axis. The paper is drawn into the process at a constant speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius of paper on the roll at any given time and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the thickness of the paper, then the angular acceleration of the roll at this instant is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0086_d7e0f635c27c.jpg\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 221px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#x3C0;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
